    <releaseNotes>
      <![CDATA[
# What's changed in Sucrose v25.10.20.0

## Announcements:
 * **Sucrose has been upgraded to .NET 9**, bringing the latest performance improvements, security updates, and modern framework features to enhance your desktop experience.
 * **The Bundle (Setup) project now uses .NET Framework 4.8** to ensure maximum backward compatibility and reliability. This framework is pre-installed on most Windows systems, providing a seamless installation experience for all users without requiring additional dependencies.

## Enhancements:
 * Some bugs have been fixed.
 * Added network online/offline status detection.
 * Processor monitoring now includes per-core load tracking.
 * Added a "Reload Wallpaper" option to the launcher context menu.
 * Centralized all `HttpClient` usage for consistent network request handling.
 * Redesigned Library and Store cards with rounded corners and updated visuals.
 * Added new monitoring support for logical and physical disk (Storage) activity and I/O.
 * Memory monitoring has been refactored to use the native `GlobalMemoryStatusEx` API.
 * Added localization support for theme titles and descriptions in the "Edit Theme" dialog.
 * Enhanced global exception handling and error reporting across all application modules.
 * Refactored environment setup to support architecture-specific .NET runtimes (x86, arm64).
 * Improved the uninstallation process with a new self-deletion mechanism for cleaner removal.
 * Added a new "Crash Mode" setting to define wallpaper behavior when `explorer.exe` crashes or restarts.
 * Replaced the internal `LocalHttpServer` with `WatsonWebServer` for serving local web content more reliably.
 * Refactored the entire hardware monitoring system for processor (CPU), graphics (GPU), memory, and storage.
 * Replaced text-based icons (e.g., 'More' button, pagination arrows) with modern `SymbolIcon` for UI consistency.
 * GPU monitoring now utilizes `Vortice.DXGI` for improved performance and accuracy, replacing the previous method.
 * Improved the robustness of inter-process communication (Pipe/Transmission) with connection timeouts, keep-alive, and retry logic.
 * The application now automatically attempts to set "High Performance" GPU preference in Windows settings for all Sucrose executables.
 * Introduced new solution-level build scripts (`.build` folder) for automated publishing, .NET runtime installation, and package compression.
 * Refactored battery, motherboard, and network data models; disabled battery/motherboard monitoring by default to improve performance.
 * Centralized build configuration and package management across the solution by adding `Directory.Build.props` and `Directory.Packages.props`.

## Translations:
 * Translations and improvements have been made.

## Updates:
 * Updated Skylark library.
 * Updated WPF-UI library.
 * Updated CsvHelper library.
 * Updated Watson.Lite library.
 * Updated Downloader library.
 * Updated Vortice.DXGI library.
 * Updated Skylark.Wing library.
 * Updated TaskScheduler library.
 * Updated HandyControls library.
 * Updated SharpCompress library.
 * Updated Skylark.Standard library.
 * Updated Skylark.Clipboard library.
 * Updated DiscordRichPresence library.
 * Updated CefSharp.Wpf.HwndHost library.
 * Updated Microsoft.Web.WebView2 library.
 * Updated WindowsAPICodePackShell library.
 * Updated Microsoft.Extensions.Hosting library.
 * Updated WPF-UI.DependencyInjection library.

## Store:
 * More than 200 new wallpaper have been added.

## Full Changelog: https://github.com/Taiizor/Sucrose/compare/v25.9.19.0...v25.10.20.0
